Z||000002||Uaana||04-05-2001||12:45 AM||||Ya I pay extortion too.<BR>The laws vary from state to state but most use a graduated system. If you make X you pay X%. The worst I've heard is in the neighbor hood of 30% but you have to make in excess of 100G for that. Bad part of this is no matter what happens to you, IE: laid off, new job pays less ect. ect. you still pay the original amount until you go back to court. If you fall too far back you get put on the credit dead beat daddy list.<BR>I can go on but I feel my B.P. rising.<BR>And before the liberals start jumping me.. I'm not opposed to paying support if the mother needs it.. I just happen to know mine has gone to adult toys like DVD player, New car payment. ect ect.<BR>I'd fight for lower payments but who can afford one after having 1/3 of their take home stripped from their check.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||04-05-2001||12:54 AM||||Okie, I agree with ya, child support is a good idea IF the other parent need it.  But like you said, it going to buy dvd players, cars and the such is wrong. child support should be done into things where they are like checks.. and can only buy certian things, like food, clothes and the such.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>child support reform! thats what we need!<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||04-05-2001||09:30 AM||||I'm in the same place. 10 years ago when mine was set, I was making $1,000 a month, they took 23% of my income *before* taxes. Left me almost nothing to live on. Wasn't even worth it to work. (and support is NOT deductable)<BR>The laws are really dumb. If you fall behind a certain amount, they report you to the credit agencies, they can suspend your license, some states even put a boot on your car. They will put you on a list to deny you a passport. And alot of that seems counter-productive to me. You take a guys license or car away, how's he supposed to work? I know one guy who fell behind, and had an opportunity at a great job, paying him probably 4 or 5 times what he had been making before, but it required some international travel, they wouldn't release his passport even though it meant he would be able to pay up his support quicker. Seems these agencies are run more on anger and revenge than on common sense.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Loki||04-05-2001||11:02 AM||||Damn..You making me wanna run away   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But it will all work out I know..She is a good mother and she will do right....Just wanted some experienses (sp?) and advice I guess....Thanx everyone<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||04-05-2001||11:54 AM||||So it isn't jsut the Australian system that is haywire then. Seen a guy out here in a Mag was living in a hovel, wife got house in divorce. She also owned a business then remarried to a highflyer on big dollars.<BR>Guy still had to live in his little hovel to battle to pay the child maintainance.<P>Not fair when it isn't need in cases like that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BENGAL4||04-05-2001||04:36 PM||||I know that some parents abuse the child support system, but some really need the income to make ends meet.<P>My late wife was one who needed the support before we got married. After the wedding, we set up a trust fund for her daughters and the child support was deposited into that. The girls can use it for their education or wait until they are 25 and use it for whatever. <P>Not one penny of child support, ever subsidized my household. I can look the girls father in the eye and tell him that. He's a piece of ****  anyway, he has seen them once in 7 years and he lives only 20 miles away. That's OK. He's their father, but I am their Dad. There is a difference.<P><BR>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 II S/C  <P>||||reg||1
